{
  "title": "47: Muhammad محمد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاَلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَضَلَّ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(1)\nLAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE AZALLAL A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThose who reject Allah and hinder (men) from the Path of Allah, their deeds will Allah render astray (from their mark). \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَاٰمَنُوْا بِمَا نُزِّلَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّهُوَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ۙ كَفَّرَ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَاَصْلَحَ بَالَهُمْ‏(2)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA AAMANOO BEMAA NUZZELA A’LAA MUHAMMADIN WA HAQQO MIN RABBEHIM KAFFARA A’NHUM SAYYEAATEHIM WAASLAHA BAALAHUM.\nBut those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, and believe in the (Revelation) sent down to Muhammad - for it is the Truth from their Lord, He will remove from them their ills and improve their condition. \nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا اتَّبَعُوا الْبَاطِلَ وَاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّبَعُوا الْحَقَّ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ اَمْثَالَهُمْ‏(3)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ATTABAU’OOA AL-BAATELA WA ANNAL LAZEENA AAMANUT ATTABAU’OOA HAQQA MIN RABBEHIM KAZAALEKA YAZREBU LAAHO LIN-NAASE AMSAALAHUM.\nThis because those who reject Allah follow vanities, while those who believe follow the Truth from their Lord: Thus does Allah set forth for men their lessons by similitudes. \nفَاِذَا لَقِيْتُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَضَرْبَ الرِّقَابِ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَاۤ اَثْخَنْتُمُوْهُمْ فَشُدُّوْا الْوَثَاقَ ۙ فَاِمَّا مَنًّۢا بَعْدُ وَاِمَّا فِدَآءً حَتّٰى تَضَعَ الْحَرْبُ اَوْزَارَهَا ۛۚ  ذٰ لِكَ ‌ۛؕ وَلَوْ يَشَآءُ اللّٰهُ لَانْتَصَرَ مِنْهُمْ  وَلٰكِنْ لِّيَبْلُوَا۟ بَعْضَكُمْ بِبَعْضٍ‌ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ قُتِلُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَلَنْ يُّضِلَّ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(4)\nFA-EZAA LAQEETUMU LAZEENA KAFAROO FAZARBA FIR REQAAB HATTAA EZAA AASKHANTUMOOHUM FASHUDDOOA AL-WASAAQA FA-IMMAA MANNAW BA’DO WA AMMAA FEDAAAN HATTAA TAZAA’A AL-HARBU AAWZAARAHAA ZAA LEKA WA LAW YASHAAA LAAHO LAANTASARA MINHUM WA LAAKIL LLEEBLOOA BAA’ZAKUM BE-BA’Z WA WAL LAZEENA QUTELOOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FALAN YYUZELLA A-A’MAALAHUM.\nTherefore, when ye meet the Unbelievers (in fight), smite at their necks; At length, when ye have thoroughly subdued them, bind a bond firmly (on them): thereafter (is the time for) either generosity or ransom: Until the war lays down its burdens. Thus (are ye commanded): but if it had been Allah's Will, He could certainly have exacted retribution from them (Himself); but (He lets you fight) in order to test you, some with others. But those who are slain in the Way of Allah, He will never let their deeds be lost. \nسَيَهْدِيْهِمْ وَيُصْلِحُ بَالَهُمْۚ‏(5)\nSAYAHDEEHEM WAYUSLEHU BAALAHUM.\nSoon will He guide them and improve their condition, \nوَيُدْخِلُهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ عَرَّفَهَا لَهُمْ‏(6)\nWAYUDKHELUHUMU JANNATA A’ARRAFAHAA LAHUM.\nAnd admit them to the Garden which He has announced for them. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنْ تَنْصُرُوا اللّٰهَ يَنْصُرْكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتْ اَقْدَامَكُمْ‏(7)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO IN TANSUROOA LAAHA YANSURKUM WAYUSABBET AAQDAAMAKUM.\nO ye who believe! If ye will aid (the cause of) Allah, He will aid you, and plant your feet firmly. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَتَعْسًا لَّهُمْ وَاَضَلَّ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(8)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO FATAA’SAN LAHUM WA AZALLAL A-A’MAALAHUM.\nBut those who reject (Allah), for them is destruction, and (Allah) will render their deeds astray (from their mark). \nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَرِهُوْا مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاَحْبَطَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(9)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAREHOOA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO FAAHBATA A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThat is because they hate the Revelation of Allah; so He has made their deeds fruitless. \nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ؕ دَمَّرَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَمْثَالُهَا‏(10)\nA-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM DAMMARA LAAHO A’LAYHIM WA LIL KAAFEREENA AAMSAALUHAA.\nDo they not travel through the earth, and see what was the End of those before them (who did evil)? Allah brought utter destruction on them, and similar (fates await) those who reject Allah. \nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَوْلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَاَنَّ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ لَا مَوْلٰى لَهُمْ‏(11)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA MAWLAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA ANNAL KAAFEREEN LAA MAWLAA LAHUM.\nThat is because Allah is the Protector of those who believe, but those who reject Allah have no protector. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يَتَمَتَّعُوْنَ وَيَاْكُلُوْنَ كَمَا تَاْكُلُ الْاَنْعَامُ وَالنَّارُ مَثْوًى لَّهُمْ‏(12)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDKHELU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YATAMATTAU’OONA WA YAAKOLOON KAMAA TAAKULU AL-AANA’AAMU WA TAMASSANAN MASWAL LAHUM.\nVerily Allah will admit those who believe and do righteous deeds, to Gardens beneath which rivers flow; while those who reject Allah will enjoy (this world) and eat as cattle eat; and the Fire will be their abode. \nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ هِىَ اَشَدُّ قُوَّةً مِّنْ قَرْيَتِكَ الَّتِىْۤ اَخْرَجَتْكَ‌ۚ اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ فَلَا نَاصِرَ لَهُمْ‏(13)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN QARYATINW HEYA ASHADDO QUWWAH MIN QARYATEKA LATEE AAKHRAJATKA AHLAKNAAHUM FALAA NAASERA LAHUM.\nAnd how many cities, with more power than thy city which has driven thee out, have We destroyed (for their sins)? and there was none to aid them. \nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ كَمَنْ زُيِّنَ لَهٗ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِهٖ وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‏(14)\nAFAMAWN KAANA A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN RABBEHI KAMAM ZUYYENA LAHU SOOO-UL A’AMALEH WAT TABA-O’O AHWAAA-AHUM.\nIs then one who is on a clear (Path) from his Lord, no better than one to whom the evil of his conduct seems pleasing, and such as follow their own lusts? \nمَثَلُ الْجَنَّةِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ‌ؕ فِيْهَاۤ اَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ غَيْرِ اٰسِنٍ‌ ۚ وَاَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ لَّبَنٍ لَّمْ يَتَغَيَّرْ طَعْمُهٗ ‌ۚ وَاَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ خَمْرٍ لَّذَّةٍ لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ ۚ وَاَنْهٰرٌ مِّنْ عَسَلٍ مُّصَفًّى‌ ؕ وَلَهُمْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ‌ؕ كَمَنْ هُوَ خَالِدٌ فِى النَّارِ وَسُقُوْا مَآءً حَمِيْمًا فَقَطَّعَ اَمْعَآءَهُمْ‏(15)\nMASALUL JANNAH LATEE WUE’EDA AL-MUTTAQOONA FEEHAA AANHAARUN MIN MAAA-IN GHAIRE AAASENIN WAANHAARUN MIN LLABANIN LAM YATAGHAYR TAA’MUH WAANHAARUN MIN KHAMRIN LLAZZATIN LLELSSHAAREBEENA WAANHAARUN MIN A’ASALIN MMUSAFFAN WA LAHUM FEEHAA MIN KULLE SAMARAATE WAMAGHFERATUN MIN RABBEHIM KAMAM HOWA KHAALEDUN FIL NAAR WASUQOOA MAAA-AN HAMEEMANW FAQATTAA’A AAMA’AAAHUM.\n(Here is) a Parable of the Garden which the righteous are promised: in it are rivers of water incorruptible; rivers of milk of which the taste never changes; rivers of wine, a joy to those who drink; and rivers of honey pure and clear. In it there are for them all kinds of fruits; and Grace from their Lord. (Can those in such Bliss) be compared to such as shall dwell for ever in the Fire, and be given, to drink, boiling water, so that it cuts up their bowels (to pieces)? \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّسْتَمِعُ اِلَيْكَ‌ۚ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا خَرَجُوْا مِنْ عِنْدِكَ قَالُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ مَاذَا قَالَ اٰنِفًا‌‌ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ طَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَ اتَّبَعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‏(16)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYASTAMEU’U ELAYKA HATTAA EZAA KHARAJOO MIN I’NDEK QAALOO LILLAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA MAA QAALA AAANEFAN OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA TABAA’A LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM WA TABA-O’O WA AHWAAA-AHUM.\nAnd among them are men who listen to thee, but in the end, when they go out from thee, they say to those who have received Knowledge, “What is it he said just then?” Such are men whose hearts Allah has sealed, and who follow their own lusts. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اهْتَدَوْا زَادَهُمْ هُدًى وَّاٰتٰٮهُمْ تَقْوٰٮهُمْ‏(17)\nWAL LAZEENA TADAW ZAADAHUM HODAM WWAATAAHUM TAQWAAHUM.\nBut to those who receive Guidance, He increases the (light of) Guidance, and bestows on them their Piety and Restraint (from evil). \nفَهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا السَّاعَةَ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمْ بَغْتَةً ‌ ۚ فَقَدْ جَآءَ اَشْرَاطُهَا‌‌ ۚ فَاَنّٰى لَهُمْ اِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ ذِكْرٰٮهُمْ‏(18)\nFA HAL YANZOROONA ILLAA SAA-A’TA AN TAATEEHUM BAGHTATANW FAQAD JAAA-A AASHRAATUHAA FA-ANNAA LAHUM EZAA JAAA-AHUM ZEKRAAHUM.\nDo they then only wait for the Hour, that it should come on them of a sudden? But already have come some tokens thereof, and when it (actually) is on them, how can they benefit then by their admonition? \nفَاعْلَمْ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنْۢبِكَ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مُتَقَلَّبَكُمْ وَمَثْوٰٮكُمْ‏(19)\nFAAA’LAM ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA LAAHO WAASTAGHFER LE-ZAMBEKA LIL-MOAMENEENA WA WA MOAMENAATE WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MUTAQALLABAKUM WAMASWAAKUM.\nKnow, therefore, that there is no god but Allah, and ask forgiveness for thy fault, and for the men and women who believe: for Allah knows how ye move about and how ye dwell in your homes. \nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ ‌ۚ فَاِذَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ مُّحْكَمَةٌ وَّذُكِرَ فِيْهَا الْقِتَالُ‌ۙ رَاَيْتَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ يَّنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ نَظَرَ الْمَغْشِىِّ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْمَوْتِ‌ؕ فَاَوْلٰى لَهُمْ‌ۚ‏(20)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA AAMANOO LAWLAA NUZZELAT SOORATUN FA-EZAA UNZELAT SOORATUN MMUHKAMATUN WWAZUKERA FEEHAA QETAALO RA-AYTA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN YYANZUROONA ELAYKA NAZARA AL-MAGHSHEAAAE A’LAYHE MENAL MAWT FAAWLAA LAHUM.\nThose who believe say, “Why is not a sura sent down (for us)?” But when a sura of basic or categorical meaning is revealed, and fighting is mentioned therein, thou wilt see those in whose hearts is a disease looking at thee with a look of one in swoon at the approach of death. But more fitting for them- \nطَاعَةٌ وَّقَوْلٌ مَّعْرُوْفٌ‌ فَاِذَا عَزَمَ الْاَمْرُ فَلَوْ صَدَقُوا اللّٰهَ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ‌ۚ‏(21)\nTAAA’ATUN WWAQAWLUN MA’ROOFUNW FA-EZAA A’AZAMA MIN FA LAW SADAQOOA LAAHA LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM.\nWere it to obey and say what is just, and when a matter is resolved on, it were best for them if they were true to Allah. \nفَهَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ اِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ اَنْ تُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوْۤا اَرْحَامَكُمْ‏(22)\nFA HAL A’SAYTUM IN TAWALLAYTUM AN TUFSEDOO FIL ARZE WATUQATTEU’OOA AARHAAMAKUM.\nThen, is it to be expected of you, if ye were put in authority, that ye will do mischief in the land, and break your ties of kith and kin? \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ فَاَصَمَّهُمْ وَاَعْمٰٓى اَبْصَارَهُمْ‏(23)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO FAASAMMAHUM WAAA’MAAA AABSAARAHUM.\nSuch are the men whom Allah has cursed for He has made them deaf and blinded their sight. \nاَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُوْنَ الْقُرْاٰنَ اَمْ عَلٰى قُلُوْبٍ اَ قْفَالُهَا‏(24)\nAFALAA YATADABBAROONA QURAANA AM A’LAA QULOOBIN AAQFAALUHAA.\nDo they not then earnestly seek to understand the Qur'an, or are their hearts locked up by them? \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ ارْتَدُّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهِمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْهُدَى‌ۙ الشَّيْطٰنُ سَوَّلَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاَمْلٰى لَهُمْ‏(25)\nINNAL LAZEENA ARTADDOOA A’LAA AADBAAREHEM MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHOMUL AL-HUDAA SHAYTAANO SAWLA LAHUM WAAMLAA LAHUM.\nThose who turn back as apostates after Guidance was clearly shown to them, the Evil One has instigated them and busied them up with false hopes. \nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ كَرِهُوْا مَا نَزَّلَ اللّٰهُ سَنُطِيْعُكُمْ فِىْ بَعْضِ الْاَمْرِۖۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اِسْرَارَهُمْ‏(26)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAALOO LILLAZEENA KAREHOOA MAA NAZZALAL LAAHO SANUTEEU’UKUM FEE BAA’ZE AL-AAMRE WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO AESRAARAHUM.\nThis, because they said to those who hate what Allah has revealed, “We will obey you in part of (this) matter”; but Allah knows their (inner) secrets. \nفَكَيْفَ اِذَا تَوَفَّتْهُمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَضْرِبُوْنَ وُجُوْهَهُمْ وَاَدْبَارَهُمْ‏(27)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA TAWAFFATHUMU TAHMELOHUL YAZREBOONA WUJOOHAHUM WAADBAARAHUM.\nBut how (will it be) when the angels take their souls at death, and smite their faces and their backs? \nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمُ اتَّبَعُوْا مَاۤ اَسْخَطَ اللّٰهَ وَكَرِهُوْا رِضْوَانَهٗ فَاَحْبَطَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(28)\nZAALEKA BEAANNAHUMU TABA-O’O WA MAA AASKHATA LAAHA WAKAREHOOA REZWAANAH FAAHBATA A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThis because they followed that which called forth the Wrath of Allah, and they hated Allah's good pleasure; so He made their deeds of no effect. \nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ اَنْ لَّنْ يُّخْرِجَ اللّٰهُ اَضْغَانَهُمْ‏(29)\nAM HASEBA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN AN LAN-Y YYUKHREJA LAAHO AAZGHAANAHUM.\nOr do those in whose hearts is a disease, think that Allah will not bring to light all their rancour? \nوَلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَاَرَيْنٰكَهُمْ فَلَعَرَفْتَهُمْ بِسِيْمٰهُمْ‌ؕ وَلَتَعْرِفَنَّهُمْ فِىْ لَحْنِ الْقَوْلِ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اَعْمَالَكُمْ‏(30)\nWA LAW NASHAAA-O LAARAYNAAKAHUM FALAA’ARAFTAHUM BESEEMAAHUM WALATAA’REFANNAHUM FEE LAHNE AL-QAWLE WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO A-A’MAALAKUM.\nHad We so wiled, We could have shown them up to thee, and thou shouldst have known them by their marks: but surely thou wilt know them by the tone of their speech! And Allah knows all that ye do. \nوَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ حَتّٰى نَعْلَمَ الْمُجٰهِدِيْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَالصّٰبِرِيْنَ ۙ وَنَبْلُوَا۟ اَخْبَارَكُمْ‏(31)\nWA LA-NABLOWANNAKUM HATTAA NAA’LAMA AL-MUJAAHEDEENA MINKUM WAS SAABEREENA WANABLOOA AAKHBAARAKUM.\nAnd We shall try you until We test those among you who strive their utmost and persevere in patience; and We shall try your reported (mettle). \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَشَآقُّوا الرَّسُوْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْهُدٰىۙ لَنْ يَّضُرُّوا اللّٰهَ شَيْئًا ؕ وَسَيُحْبِطُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ‏(32)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAAHA YATTABE-U’R MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHOMUL HODAA LAN YYAZURROOA LAAHA SHAY-ANW WASAYUHBETU A-A’MAALAHUM.\nThose who reject Allah, hinder (men) from the Path of Allah, and resist the Messenger, after Guidance has been clearly shown to them, will not injure Allah in the least, but He will make their deeds of no effect. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَلَا تُبْطِلُوْۤا اَعْمَالَكُمْ‏(33)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R WA LAA TUBTELOO A-A’MAALAKUM.\nO ye who believe! Obey Allah, and obey the messenger, and make not vain your deeds! \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ مَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ فَلَنْ يَّغْفِرَ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ‏(34)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WASADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE SUMMA MAATOOA WA HUM KUFFAARUN FALAN YAGHFERAL LAAHO LAHUM.\nThose who reject Allah, and hinder (men) from the Path of Allah, then die rejecting Allah, Allah will not forgive them. \nفَلَا تَهِنُوْا وَتَدْعُوْۤا اِلَى السَّلْمِ‌ۖ وَاَنْتُمُ الْاَعْلَوْنَ‌ۖ وَاللّٰهُ مَعَكُمْ وَلَنْ يَّتِرَكُمْ اَعْمَالَكُمْ‏(35)\nFALAA TAHENOOA WATADU’OOA ELAL AS-SALME WAANTUMU AL-AAA’LAWNA WAL LAAHO MA-A’KUM WA LAN YYATERAKUM A-A’MAALAKUM.\nBe not weary and faint-hearted, crying for peace, when ye should be uppermost: for Allah is with you, and will never put you in loss for your (good) deeds. \nاِنَّمَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا لَعِبٌ وَّلَهْوٌ‌ ؕ وَاِنْ تُؤْمِنُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا يُؤْتِكُمْ اُجُوْرَكُمْ وَلَا يَسْئَلْكُمْ اَمْوَالَكُمْ‏(36)\nINNAMAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA LAE’EBUN WWALAHWUN WA LAM TOAMENOO WA TATTAQOO YUTEKUM AUJOORAKUM WA LAA YASALKUM AMWAALAKUM.\nThe life of this world is but play and amusement: and if ye believe and guard against Evil, He will grant you your recompense, and will not ask you (to give up) your possessions. \nاِنْ يَّسْئَلْكُمُوْهَا فَيُحْفِكُمْ تَبْخَلُوْا وَيُخْرِجْ اَضْغَانَكُمْ‏(37)\nIN YYASALKUMOOHAA FAYUHFEKUM TABKHALOOA WA YUKHRIJ AAZGHAANAKUM.\nIf He were to ask you for all of them, and press you, ye would covetously withhold, and He would bring out all your ill-feeling. \nهٰۤاَنْتُمْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ تُدْعَوْنَ لِتُنْفِقُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ‌ۚ فَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يَّبْخَلُ ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ يَّبْخَلْ فَاِنَّمَا يَبْخَلُ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ الْغَنِىُّ وَاَنْتُمُ الْفُقَرَآءُ ‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَتَوَلَّوْا يَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْ ۙ ثُمَّ لَا يَكُوْنُوْۤا اَمْثَالَكُم‏(38)\nHAANTUM HAAOOLAAA-E TUDA’AWNA LE-TUNFEQOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA MINKUM MAN YYABKHALU WA MAN YYABKHAL FA-INNAMAA YABKHALU A’N NNAFSEH WAL LAAHO AL-GHANEAAAU WAANTUMU AL-FUQARAAU WA IN YASTABDEL QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM SUMMA LAA YAKOONOOA AAMSAALAKUM.\nBehold, ye are those invited to spend (of your substance) in the Way of Allah: But among you are some that are niggardly. But any who are niggardly are so at the expense of their own souls. But Allah is free of all wants, and it is ye that are needy. If ye turn back (from the Path), He will substitute in your stead another people; then they would not be like you!",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 37 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that whoever recites this Surah will have his thirst quenched by the drink from the rivers of Jannah.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) said that the person who recites this Surah will never have doubts about his religion and will not fall into disbelief and Shirk. A thousand angels will send salutations to his grave after his death. He will be placed under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) and His Prophet (s.a.w.a.). When the reciter of this Surah will arise from his grave, whichever way he turns, he will see the blessed face of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIf this Surah is written and kept as a talisman, it protects a person, whether he is asleep or awake, from all evils and problems. It is also a safety from insanity."
